From: dtrace.nix maintainers
Subject: btf,fbt: index function types and reject noreturn returns

FBT population visits every traceable kernel symbol.  Looking up each symbol
by linearly scanning the complete BTF table makes wildcard probe discovery
quadratic.  Build a compact sorted name-and-kind index lazily and use binary
search instead.

Linux also rejects fexit attachment to an explicit set of noreturn functions;
mirror that set while retaining their valid entry probes.

